.convert-temp
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.tps
*.tcp
*.log
*.out
*.aux
*.synctex
# xelatex's `-recorder` log, which belongs with the three above it: the build's own land in
# `output/`, which is ignored anyway, and the ones that turn up in the working directory are
# droppings of a run that was not this build -- five of them sat in the root for a week
# because this family had every TeX suffix but that one.
*.fls
# dvisvgm's extracted glyph outlines. It writes `font-XXXX.cff` into the *working directory*
# rather than beside its output, so a run of `core/html/mathimage.py` from the root leaves them
# there -- seven of them sat in the root for two days. `--no-fonts` is passed and is why the
# SVGs carry paths rather than font references; it does not stop the extraction itself.
font-*.cff
*.pyc
*__pycache__*
*.dblite
.idea/
build/

# The Ninja spike (`tools/ninja/generate.py`). The graph is generated, never written by hand,
# and `.ninja_log` / `.ninja_deps` are Ninja's own state beside it.
build.ninja
.ninja_log
.ninja_deps
render/
output/
source/
# ...and note those four are bare patterns, so they match a directory of that name at *any*
# depth, not only at the root. That once silently excluded a vendored `…/output/` directory
# from a commit, and `git status` says nothing, because an ignored file is not untracked.
_*/
.idea/*
svg-inkscape/
*.minted

# `npm ci` fetches these; see package.json. The HTML output needs MathJax at build time.
node_modules/
